dxnotepad seems very slow to echo the user's input when the document
gets moderately large (10 seconds in a 30 page document).

Our users on a Digital Unix Alpha 3000/600 running 

DEC OSF/1 V3.0 (Rev. 347); Sat Apr 22 01:08:58 PDT 1995 
DEC OSF/1 V3.0 Worksystem Software (Rev. 347)

have complained about the slowness of character-echo during dxnotepad
when 30-page documents are edited.
I presume that dxnotepad has very inefficient memory usage and is moving
the whole document in memory to make room for the new characters.
I have confirmed this by verifying that insertion at the beginning of 
a pre-existing 150Kbyte document takes up to 30 seconds, 
whereas at the end of the document, insertion is instantaneous.
But still, taking 30 seconds to shift 150Kbytes by 5 or 10 bytes seems
outrageous on a system where swapping is not happening.

Does anyone know whether dxnotepad speed has improved in later versions ?
Or should we give up on dxnotepad as a routine editor ?

