Dear Colleagues,

here is a common mail problem under OSF/1 (I'd guess): 

On our machines, we simply use family names as login names. This implies,
of course, that names with more than 8 characters have to be truncated or
otherwise abbreviated, e.g. jaro for jarochewsky.

Now the problem: the user would of course like to be reachable under his 
real name, e.g.

  jaroschewsky@uke.uni-hamburg.de

For incoming mail, this is easily done, adding the line

jaroschewsky:	jaro

to the sendmail aliases file. For outgoing mail, however, his name appears
on the From: line still as

  jaro@uke.uni-hamburg.de

Even though this does not really limit functionality, it confuses many of
our users. Therefore, I would like to rewrite (sendmail rules?) the From: 
address, preferably using the information already present in the aliases
file. 

