Ah yes... DECnsr... Another one with problems. Watch out of you let the
install put /var as a symbolic link to /usr/var, and then add filesystems
to be mounted as /var/whatever

You'll notice (Probably when you goto restore) that the filesystems aren't
in your backups... Major Bummer...

Take a look... The filesystems in fstab to be mounted at /var/whatever,
will actually get mounted at /usr/var/whatever, that I can live with. What
I don't like is the way DECnsr silently decides to ignore the
filesystems. Probably if you only have 1 machine you'd notice. Maybe. When
you rely on separate people creating filesystems, and checking the backup
completion messages, things don't get seen unless its flagged as an
error...


: I know some folks have had problems with advfs but we have experienced none.

Lucky you. In todays world, I think people should be more demanding that a
machine shouldn't go belly-up just becasue a disk isn't 100% correct. Last
I saw do that (Beside DEC) was a Sun with a bad floppy... I think they
fixed that. pity DEC aren't interested in doing it to their code...



