Don Wilkerson (don@colosys.net) wrote:
: How do I create another account, for emergency only, that would have
: super-user priviliges.  That last time I tried adding a user called 'newsu'
: and gave it a uid of '0' all my owner names changed from 'root' to 'newsu'.
: I don't want it to do that.

There's a great program out there called sudo.  Using a configuration 
file, you can give it a list of users who may have root privelages (and,
optionally, which programs they are allowed to run as root).  After that,
the user can type
  sudo <command>
to run the command as root.  If it has been more than five minutes since
the last running of sudo by that user, it prompts the user for his/her
password, incase they walked away from their terminal.

