The Korn, Bourne and C shells are supported under
Solaris 2.4.

At the prompt, enter: ksh, sh, csh to access the respective
shells.

To default to a specific shell, select the default shell
when you create new users using admintool.

You can also manually change your shell by editing the 
/etc/passwd file.

