technical@netcat.com wrote:
: Can someone tell me if OSF/1 currently supports the ATT DLPI specification.
: If so, what is the name of the device (usually is /dev/DLPI)?  Also, is
: promiscious mode operations supported and is the DLPI API autoloaded
: into the kernel.

:   Ted Hulick/technical@netcat.com
DEC OSF/1 (DIGITAL UNIX) does support DLPI spec. It's  a kernel subsystem
and is added into the kernel by adding the following statement in the
system configuration file :

    options        DLPI

Rebuild the kernel using the doconfig utility.
This way the /dev/streams/dlpi STREAMS pseudo-device driver
is configured into the kernel and is available to be used as a
standard STREAMS driver. However, the DLPI implementation on
DEC OSF/1 3.2 does NOT support promiscious mode operatons.

Cheers !!




