>Hello,
>	Does anybody have the /etc/disktab entry for the Seagate 9 GB
>disk? (or for any 9 Gig disk). Just got one and I can't get the
>disklabel right :).

Is it really necessary to have a disktab entry?  I've found that

	disklabel -rz rz3 i-dont-have-a-disktab

works fine for me.  If disklabel can't find a tag in the disktab
that matches "i-dont-have-a-disktab", then disklabel will poll the
disk for its size and build a partition table that I can edit with
"disklabel -e", if I want to.

From the disklabel man page:
>If your disk type is not specified in the /etc/disktab file, disklabel
>uses the default partition information in the driver.

Has anyone had problems with using the default partitioning?

Paul Fardy
