>>>>> "JA" == Jorn Amundsen <joern@sima.sintef.no> writes:
In article <JOERN.95Aug15172911@nazgul.sima.sintef.no> joern@sima.sintef.no (Jorn Amundsen) writes:


JA> After upgrading our 3000/400 to DEC Unix v.3.2 this simple aio program
JA> below seems not to work anymore. It works without problems on SGI
JA> systems. It bails out before reaching the first executable line of
JA> code with:

JA> 	$ cc  -g -o taio taio.c -laio -lpthreads
JA> 	dbx taio
JA> 	dbx version 3.11.8
JA> 	Type 'help' for help.

Thanks to Digital for a fast reply on this one! Here it is:

Actually, the above works by accident on releases earlier than
3.2. The correct way to compile and link applications using threads is

	$ cc  -g -o taio taio.c -laio -threads

which includes -lpthreads and any thread safe versions of other implicitly
(like libc.a) and explicitly specified libraries.

--joern


