I do dumps (actually vdumps) all the time in multi-user mode. dump works
fine in multi-user mode, but any files that get changed while the dump
happens may confuse dump, as well as providing a non-consistent backup.

> 2) What do other Unix sites use (especially Ultrix or OSF/1 sites) to get 
> reliable backups while in multi-user mode ?

POLYCENTER Networker Save and Restore. You can backup multiple clients
to a single tape drive at the same time. Digital UNIX 3.2 has a
"SingleServer" version bundled: you can backup one client (itself) to
the NSR server (itself again).

The full-blown version uses the network to backup the clients to the
server, but this is seen as an advantage. 8-) You can use compression
to decrease network bandwidth if you want to.

PJDM
