mpham@alpha.tricity.wsu.edu wrote:
: Hi,
: My system (name COOL) is a DEC Alpha 400 OSF1 v3.2a.  I have a program that
: fork a lots
: of child processes when it run.  However, the maximum of child processes I
: can run for that program is 64.  What should I do to increase number of
: child process.  I tried to increase the number of CHILD_MAX in
: /sys/include/sys/syslimits.h.  I also tried to add a line "maxuprc 640"
: in my /sys/conf/COOL file. After each try, I rebuild the kernal (config,
: make), cp new vmunix to / and reboot the machine but I still can not
: increase the number of child process.  Please tell me what I should do.
: Thank in advance for your help.

Sounds like you need to increase your 'max-proc-per-user' limit in the
'proc' subsystem of /etc/sysconfigtab.  (Although I would think that
your "maxuprc 640" entry in your config file would have done this --
but it won't hurt to try).  The default is 64.  You can check the
current value by doing "sysconfig -q proc".

The man page for sysconfigtab(4) shows the exact entry you need.  After
making this change, reboot.

Tim
