organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
reply-to: eklund@fman.zko.dec.com (Dave Eklund)
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

	I can only speak for DEC Fortran where you can get a call to
sincos out of a code fragment like:

        do i=1,100
        type *,sin(float(i)),cos(float(i))
        enddo
        end
 
	The compiler recognizes the need for both the sin and cos values,
and generates code accordingly, picking up the values from the appropriate
registers.  I believe that DEC C does the same thing with similar code.

Dave Eklund



