Bassirou> from the console prompt.

Bassirou> sh dev  shows
Bassirou> 	mkd500.5.0.5.0 MKD500 TZ87 9719

Bassirou> When I run ./MAKEDEV tz20 I am able to create /dev/rm??? device

Bassirou> but file /dev/rmt0h gives only 
Bassirou> /dev/rmt0h:     character special (9/37890)
Bassirou> as output

Bassirou> and mt status give 
Bassirou> /dev/nrmt0h: I/O error

Have you properly configured your kernel so that it knows about all
four SCSI controllers you have on your system?  I'm not really
familiar with 8000 series alphas, but on the AS 2100 and 3000 series
machines, SCSI chains are lettered from dkaxxx, dkbxxx, ... on up.  

The simplest way for you to add this device to your system is to
follow the directions given in the 'doconfig' man page for adding new
hardware.  It's a pretty easy set of steps to follow.

Once you have done those steps, you need to redo the ./MAKEDEV
command.  Assuming you have the four SCSI busses, and you keep the
tape drive a ID 5, you would use device 'tz29', (the math is: 8x4+5).

This should get you going.

