In article <807926200snz@osil.demon.co.uk>, Dave Herdman <dherdman@osil.demon.co.uk> writes:
|> Hi
|> 
|> I have just discovered an alpha PC 150 in a closet that was used 
|> for a WIN NT evaluation a few years back. It has 32 meg of mem
|> will it  run OSF/1 ( subject to getting the licence etc) ?
|> 

Yes, but it may need adjustment. If it is the _standard_ PC 150 with 
Compaq QVision video board, Adaptec SCSI, etc. it is capable of running
OSF/1, so long as the Adaptec board has the "G2" ROM revision. Initial ships
of the system had only a "G" revision - I had three of them. "G" chips
(at least on mine) are labelled "ADAPTEC INC 450128-00E698 MCODE BG46 (c)
1993".

Other equipment may or may not work (I can't say...)

32Mb I feel is borderline for a "usable" system under OSF/1. Fine for fast
X display _or_ low memory programs, but I wouldn't load it too much.


