Howdy!
I had the same problem during my compilation of elm for OSF. The following
should fix it:

defs.h.orig: Line about 654

#ifdef POSIX_SIGNALS
#define signal posix_signal
#if ANSI_C
extern SIGHAND_TYPE (*posix_signal(int, SIGHAND_TYPE (*)(int)))(int);
#else   /* ANSI_C */
extern SIGHAND_TYPE (*posix_signal())();
#endif  /* ANSI_C */

defs.h.fixed:

#ifdef POSIX_SIGNALS
#define signal posix_signal
#if ANSI_C
extern SIGHAND_TYPE (*posix_signal(int, SIGHAND_TYPE (*)(int)))(int);
#endif  /* ANSI_C */

Sorry that I didn't post a diff, but I did not have the original
file I patched, instead had to ftp new elm-sources, which differed much
more than in these few lines :-((.
I hope it helped anyway, if not, email me.
