Recently, we have purchased a Digital DLT2000 magnetic tape drive and
a DLT2700 Mini-library (7 slots). We have plugged it to an IBM RS/6000
workstation running AIX 3.2.5 and we are using the "standard" SCSI
tape driver supplied with AIX.
 
The first thing we wanted to test was the basic operations of the tape
drive (open,read,write,close,rew,fsf,...), not yet the mini-library
operations.  That worked fine. Now we want to use some features supported
by this kind of drives, such as the READ POSITION,LOCATE,
READ BLOCK LIMITS, LOG SENSE... SCSI commands, but the only means
to do that with the SCSI driver we have in AIX is to open the drive
in Extension mode ("openx" system call) having 'root' authority,
build and send the the SCSI command directly to the device, which
makes virtually unusable this sort of interesting features for any
normal user application 8-(.
 
So, my question is: is there a SCSI device driver for the DLT2000 for
the AIX 3.2.x operation system? If so, who should we contact for
obtaining it? If there is no such a driver, and provided that we
want/have to use the sort of features mentionned above, should we
purchase a Digital ALPHA running OSF/1 in order do do that (assuming that
the driver exists for the Digital machines -- is this true?) ?
 
Any help with this problem will be very appreciated. Thanks in advance.
 
Fabio.
 
