>>>>> "David" == David Tagget <73772.3727@CompuServe.COM> writes:
In article <3vmeqk$kap$1@mhadf.production.compuserve.com> David Tagget <73772.3727@CompuServe.COM> writes:


David> Can anyone tell me how to config the DEFPA-AA PCI FDDI card
David> with a Digital Alpha station running Digital UNIX(OSF)?

You need to build a new kernel with the proper entries for the card,
then you need to run 'netsetup' to configure the fta0: network
device.  On our 2100 5/250 the kernel entry looks like this:

	controller  fta0 at pci0 slot 6 vector ftaintr

The number the has to change is the slot # depending on which PCI slot
the card is in.  Your system hardware guide should give you the
mappings.  If you already have some PCI options installed, you should
be able to figure out what goes where.  

The other method is to boot with genvmunix instead of vmunix, then run
'doconfig' to build a new kernel.  See the man page for the full
details.

