>How does one change the screen resolution of an application when it is
>starting up under Motif?  This is for SunOS...  I believe it is in the
>'Xdefaults' file but don't know exactly where.
>
The screen resolution is not an application resource, so .Xdefaults
isn't very likely to help.  It is the X server which handles the
screen resolution, but most video hardware supports only one (fixed
frequency monitors).  The only server which allows changing the
resolution on the fly that I know of is XFree86, available on most
Unices for PC's.

BTW, Motif has nothing to do with your problem and this newsgroup is
_not_ for SunOS...

Dan
