After you installed your DEFPA-AA start your system and make a new 
kernel with the command

	doconfig

review your config file /sys/conf/HOSTNAME.
A line similar to 

controller      fta0       at pci0      slot  7 vector    ftaintr

should now be in it.

It it's not edit the file and make the new kernel with

	doconfig -c HOSTNAME


Copy or move the new kernel to /.

Reboot your system.

Now you should be able to configure your FDDI network interface with the
setup script.

Enter setup and choos 'Internet Networking' and follow the instructions.


