V1.4 (I think) which was exposed by Digital UNIX V3.2 which would cause
some MPEG files to stop after displaying the first frame.

The current version of Multimedia Services is V1.6.  Try upgrading to
that to see if it fixes your problem.  If you are still having problems,
send me some more details on your problem such as the version of software
that you are running, the differences between the files that work and those
that don't (or examples of files that don't) and I'll look into it in more
detail.

In addition to the substantial performance increase that you noticed with
AlphaVCR over 'mpeg_play', you also get support for MPEG-1 Systems streams
including MPEG-1 audio as well as a slider for random access to different
parts of the file.

