In article <top.3.301D05EC@ccrs.emr.ca>, top@ccrs.emr.ca (Andrew Top) writes:
>
>   My hard-drive on an Alpha running OSF1 1.3 (old I know) must
>have a loose connection.  It disappeared a few weeks ago but now
>at the console prompt (>>>) a show device shows that is does 
>exist.  The disk rz9 is the problem disk.
>
>DKA000      rz8     2.1 GB
>DKA100      rz9     2.1 GB
>DKA200      rz10    2.1 GB
>
>    Do I need to do a disklabel before trying to mount it?

No.  While the drive may have disappeared, it is unlikely the
data did.  What was there before is probably still there.

If the operating system can't see it then you have a hardware
problem somewhere in the chain.  Check the cable connections,
bus termination, etc.  Try taking the other drives out what
the suspicious one is the only thing on the bus.  Add the others
back one at a time.

If you're using StorageWorks devices, they get their SCSI ID
from the shelf.  If the shelf has a problem is giving two
drives the same address, then one will "disappear".
--
Alan Rollow				alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com




